    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d340-a3">

                <pb facs="0796" n="748" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg748"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Coat of arms of the United States.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Decree.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Yokohama,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 26, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>In pursuance of the 4th section of the act of Congress giving certain judicial
                    powers, &amp;c., approved June 22, 1850, I, Robert B. Van Valkenburgh, minister
                    resident of the United States in Japan, do hereby decree the following
                    regulation, which shall have the force of law in the courts of the United States
                    in Japan.</p>
                <p>The act of Congress to prohibit the coolie trade, &amp;c., approved February 19,
                    1862, and which was framed with regard to China, is hereby made applicable to
                    Japan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">[seal.]</hi> R. B. VAN VALKENBURGH, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United States in
                            Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
